  body: "# State scheme pension credit: State Pension sharing\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nIn the pension-sharing
    section, state scheme pension credit means an amount received from a spouse or civil partner under a pension
    sharing court order, and is linked to shared SP on divorce or dissolution.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThis
    phrase is not an alias for the means-tested Pension Credit benefit. Old and new state scheme pension credits,
    court-order dates, pensionable age and valuation/revaluation rules must be kept distinct. No financial-settlement
    calculation is provided.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 74451, PDF page 54](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f255d3e08b8871b665ab/dmg-Ch-74.pdf#page=54).\n\
    - [DMG 74452, PDF page 54](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f255d3e08b8871b665ab/dmg-Ch-74.pdf#page=54).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch74` — PDF SHA-256 `5961a9cb7c86814a0f6fa147c0a8a551b4258c803680fac14a95cab9eca1afd6`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `c762e93940b4342d70d5bc96a80c3e094c91852d93868f5709e04f293faef61a`.\n"
