    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch74/0054
      quote: "74452 A person is entitled to a shared SP on divorce or dissolution if they\n\n\n1. have reached pensionable
        age and\n\n\n2. are entitled to a state scheme pension credit1.\n\n\nNote 1: A state scheme pension credit
        can be a new or old state scheme pension credit 2. It is an amount\na spouse or civil partner receives from
        the other spouse or civil partner under a pension sharing court\n\norder3.\n\n\nNote 2: See DMG 74022 for
        the meaning of pensionable age.\n\n\nNote 3: See DMG Chapter 75 for guidance on how old state scheme pension
        credit affects RP.\n\n\n                                    1 Pensions Act 14, s 13(1); 2 s 13(6); 3 WRP
        Act 99, s 49(1)(b) & 49A(2)(b)"
      locator: DMG 74452
